1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:45,128
We kissed.

3
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:13,198
My very first kiss…

4
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:20,580
wasn't anything like the ones
in books or dramas.

5
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:23,416
No bells. No sparks.

6
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,043
But…

7
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:58,118
the time…

8
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,703
flew by so ****ing fast.

9
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:02,872
It's morning already.

10
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:36,990
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

11
00:02:40,118 --> 00:02:41,494
Come out.

12
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:42,954
I can see you.

13
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:48,126
Oh.

14
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:50,211
You're here.

15
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:53,548
Why'd you hide?

16
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:55,925
No, I wasn't hiding.

17
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:58,803
The table looked a bit wobbly,

18
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,597
so I was just checking.

19
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,307
It's fine now.

20
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:07,312
Ms. Na.

21
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,022
Yes?

22
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:13,860
I…

23
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:17,989
Is he about to ask me out
now that we've kissed?

24
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:19,616
Or

25
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,160
does he want another kiss?

26
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:27,457
It's a kiss.

27
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,667
…need

28
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:31,419
a charge.

29
00:03:33,671 --> 00:03:34,505
What?

30
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:37,592
A charge.

31
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:39,886
Oh.

32
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:44,724
Right, a charge.

33
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,684
A charge.

34
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:49,270
What were you imagining?

35
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:51,773
What? Imagine what?

36
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:53,816
Let's go. I'll charge you.

37
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:12,961
What? Where are you going?
You said you needed a charge.

38
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:18,132
Let's do it here.

39
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:22,428
In your room.

40
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:30,937
This is

41
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:33,982
my room?

42
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,652
Don't say no this time.

43
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:54,294
You should stay in the house.
Stop living in the garage.

44
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:07,974
What are you doing?

45
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:11,227
I'm just grateful for everything.

46
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:17,108
Consider it a bonus charge.

47
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:24,490
You were supposed to charge me anyway.

48
00:05:29,662 --> 00:05:31,789
Seriously?
You always do whatever you want.

49
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:37,003
All right, we're done.

50
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:38,546
That's enough!

51
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:54,395
We should apologize to Ms. Na, right?

52
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:58,649
Should I talk to her first?

53
00:05:58,733 --> 00:05:59,567
Yeah.

54
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:05,323
Ms. Na.

55
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,909
-Yes?
-Well…

56
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:10,578
It's almost lunchtime.

57
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:13,164
If you don't have lunch plans
with Mr. Baek,

58
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:15,583
would you like to join us?

59
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:17,960
Sure.

60
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:18,920
Wait.

61
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,963
You always have lunch with Mr. Baek.

62
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:22,632
Are you sure that's okay?

63
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:24,550
Yes, it's totally fine.

64
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:27,762
Great! Let's go have something nice.

65
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:28,930
Sounds good.

66
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:35,061
Who said you could do that?

67
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:47,240
Wow.

68
00:06:47,323 --> 00:06:50,993
It's been a long time
since we had lunch together, sir.

69
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:53,037
We just had a team dinner in Jeju.

70
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,289
Yes. You're right.

71
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,208
We did. Silly me.

72
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,460
Lunch with Ms. Na

73
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:03,005
was part of my routine.

74
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:05,425
But she agreed
to have lunch with you so readily.

75
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,135
That surprised me.

76
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:09,595
Sir.

77
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:12,473
We felt like we owed her an apology,

78
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:14,308
so we asked her to lunch.

79
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:18,312
Well, you see…

80
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:21,023
When the rumors about you and Mr. Ji
started spreading,

81
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:24,193
I believed them and treated you coldly.
I'm sorry.

82
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:25,820
I'm really sorry.

83
00:07:25,903 --> 00:07:29,449
I mean, they even figured out
you were a drama writer, so--

84
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:31,742
I'm really sorry.

85
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:33,369
I'm sorry.

86
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,954
No, don't be.

87
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:39,292
It's hard to know what to believe
with rumors like that. I understand.

88
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:41,919
How could you judge someone like that?

89
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,464
Reflect on your actions.

90
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:49,469
It's really okay. Please enjoy your meal.

91
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:54,557
Ms. Na.

92
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:59,520
Do you really have no feelings
for Mr. Ji Eun-ho?

93
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:07,236
Well…

94
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:09,697
Yes.

95
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:14,285
Eun-ho's just a close friend.
He's like a little brother to me.

96
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:15,328
That's all.

97
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,830
I mean, he's handsome,

98
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:19,832
younger than you,

99
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:24,462
and a huge star
who would do anything for you.

100
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:26,672
If you're not interested in him,

101
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:30,676
I'm curious to know
what your ideal type is like.

102
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,178
Wow.

103
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:35,473
I've never heard Mr. Yoon ask
a question like that.

104
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:36,390
Huh?

105
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:39,769
Could it be that he has a crush on Ms. Na?

106
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:47,109
I'm just curious.

107
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,612
No ulterior motives.

108
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:53,407
My ideal type…

109
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:58,329
If I say anything
that sounds like Mr. Baek,

110
00:08:58,412 --> 00:08:59,705
they'll figure me out.

111
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:05,253
Well, for starters, I…

112
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:11,384
-I like free spirits.
-"Free"?

113
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:13,970
You know,
someone who's a big P on the MBTI.

114
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:18,099
Someone who makes impulsive decisions
and just takes off on trips.

115
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:19,183
"Impulsive"?

116
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,936
Someone a bit younger than me

117
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,231
with a fair, baby face.

118
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:27,900
Chubby cheeks that stretch
when you pinch them.

119
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,318
Right. A face like tofu.

120
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,486
Tofu face.

121
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:31,445
"Tofu"?

122
00:09:31,529 --> 00:09:33,197
And I like someone

123
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:36,867
with no muscles at all.

124
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:39,954
I like them skinny. Like a twig.

125
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:42,915
So that's why Mr. Ji didn't make the cut.

126
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:45,167
Exactly. Eun-ho has muscles.

127
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:47,753
You seem quite particular

128
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:50,673
about your ideal man.

129
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:53,968
Yeah, I have high standards.

130
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,150
What are you doing?

131
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:12,903
Should I lose some weight and muscle?

132
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:13,821
Sorry?

133
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:15,948
Do I have too much muscle?

134
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:19,535
Wait, but I need chubbier cheeks.

135
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:21,871
-How am I supposed to--
-Sir.

136
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:26,292
-What?
-The TS succession is imminent.

137
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:27,335
You need to focus.

138
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:32,632
Who says I'm not focused?

139
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:42,266
Did you give them the slush fund ledger?

140
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:46,062
Yes. Doseong Daily will handle the rest.

141
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:50,024
They should've hidden their weaknesses
before attacking me.

142
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:55,112
They've got so many enemies.
How dare they challenge me?

143
00:10:55,821 --> 00:10:56,656
Mr. Yoon.

144
00:10:57,823 --> 00:10:58,866
Sir?

145
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,994
What's "a big P" in MBTI?

146
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:02,912
Sorry?

147
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:05,206
Ms. Na mentioned it earlier.

148
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:10,378
She said she likes
people with a big P in MBTI.

149
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:11,295
Sir.

150
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:13,506
I have to get back to work.

151
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:15,841
I must attend to a very important matter

152
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:18,260
to get ready
for the succession of TS Group.

153
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:42,326
A BIG P IN MBTI

154
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:01,887
BACK VIEW OF I-HYEOK STANDING
IN THE MEETING ROOM

155
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:07,977
What is it?

156
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,061
(NERVOUSLY)

157
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:11,272
(PULLING HYE-JU TOWARDS HIM)

158
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:12,273
Just a moment.

159
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:18,195
What is it? Is there someone suspicious?

160
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,989
-Am I in danger?
-No.

161
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:20,906
(GAZING TENDERLY)

162
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,201
Even if you were,
I would never let anyone hurt you.

163
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:26,954
Why did you ask me to come here?

164
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:28,664
No reason.

165
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:29,582
(GAZING INTENSELY)

166
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:31,375
(FLUSTERED)

167
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:34,754
I-HYEOK PUSHES HYE-JU AGAINST THE WALL

168
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:37,214
HYE-JU'S HEART RACES, READY TO BURST

169
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:39,300
I just

170
00:12:40,050 --> 00:12:41,635
wanted to see you.

171
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:43,429
Is that not okay?

172
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:44,805
(SEDUCTIVELY)

173
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:50,478
I-HYEOK LEANS IN TOWARD HYE-JU'S LIPS

174
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:52,146
HYE-JU SURRENDERS TO HIM

175
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:53,105
Ms. Na!

176
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:54,356
Ms. Na!

177
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:55,900
Yes?

178
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:05,785
A moment of your time, please.

179
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:24,261
What is it?

180
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:26,639
Just a moment.

181
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:31,268
Isn't this exactly what I just wrote
in my script?

182
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,280
What are you doing all of a sudden?

183
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,032
I

184
00:13:45,616 --> 00:13:46,617
looked it up.

185
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:49,286
Looked what up?

186
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:55,459
A big P in MBTI.

187
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:58,629
In the Myers–Briggs Type Indicator,

188
00:13:58,712 --> 00:14:00,506
P stands for perceiving.

189
00:14:00,589 --> 00:14:04,301
It refers to people
with a strong tendency to perceive.

190
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,178
Oh.

191
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,721
Yes.

192
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:14,270
P types tend to be free-spirited,
flexible, exploratory,

193
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,647
and spontaneous.

194
00:14:17,606 --> 00:14:19,316
Are you giving a presentation?

195
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:24,530
-Why are you standing like--
-I asked for you on a whim.

196
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,323
Openly hitting on you at work.

197
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:28,325
It's not easy

198
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:31,662
for a senior managing director
at a major corporation

199
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:34,665
to be this flexible.

200
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:36,333
I don't think

201
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:38,377
this is really a P thing.

202
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,503
Really?

203
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:43,507
How about this?

204
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:44,675
What?

205
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:57,021
Will you go out with me?

206
00:14:59,064 --> 00:14:59,899
What?

207
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,609
I haven't asked you out yet.

208
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,070
Let's date.

209
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:07,865
Even after our contract ends,

210
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:10,159
let's stay together.

211
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:21,170
Didn't expect that, did you?
Spontaneous and free-spirited, right?

212
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:23,756
No, it's not that.

213
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,299
I just…

214
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:32,056
Since we already kissed,

215
00:15:32,806 --> 00:15:34,475
I thought we were dating.

216
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:35,643
What?

217
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:38,437
Oh.

218
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:42,942
No, you're right. You're absolutely right.

219
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:44,652
No, it's just…

220
00:15:44,735 --> 00:15:50,366
Earlier, you said your ideal type
was a free-spirited, spontaneous P-type.

221
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:51,700
Right?

222
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:54,453
Ms. Na Bo-bae?

223
00:15:55,829 --> 00:15:57,623
What is it?

224
00:15:58,624 --> 00:15:59,875
Why are you laughing?

225
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,544
Oh, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

226
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:04,129
How are you this cute?

227
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:08,092
Cute? What do you mean?

228
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,386
Don't you mean "cool"?

229
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:12,429
No, you're really cute.

230
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:15,057
Cute? I'm a grown man.

231
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:17,768
Aw, is Ho-rang angry like a tiger?

232
00:16:17,851 --> 00:16:19,103
Poor baby.

233
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:20,729
Rawr.

234
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:26,318
Ms. Na Bo-bae.
I take back what I said earlier.

235
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,280
Mr. Baek…

236
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:31,824
Mr. Baek Ho-rang, wait.

237
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:42,334
Gosh, Baek Ho-rang is so cute.

238
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,460
Seriously.

239
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:48,048
"So cute"?

240
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,551
Wow, that's so cringe.

241
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:55,264
Then again, he was the one
who started acting all cute.

242
00:16:56,432 --> 00:17:00,310
I mean, how can a grown man be so cute?

243
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:03,439
Seriously.

244
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,611
Will you go out with me?

245
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:22,332
Huh?

246
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:27,171
No. Stop that.

247
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:30,507
Darn it.

248
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:31,425
Ms. Na.

249
00:17:32,676 --> 00:17:35,345
I can feel it. This is going to be a hit.

250
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,431
You've got yourself a contract!

251
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:40,059
Oh my gosh! Director!

252
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:40,976
Ms. Na!

253
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,312
For real? My gosh!

254
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:47,816
I knew you could do it.

255
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:52,404
Look at you.

256
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:57,367
Do I smell?

257
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:02,372
Let's really lock in.

258
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,333
I'll give this project my all.

259
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:21,141
Man, this is…

260
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,645
This is why experience matters.

261
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:27,648
Just write it down as is,
and it's a drama.

262
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:35,340
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

263
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:38,260
You should have breakfast.

264
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:40,220
Okay?

265
00:19:44,683 --> 00:19:45,934
Come on. Wake up.

266
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:48,437
Open up.

267
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,365
Okay, that's it.

268
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:02,993
You're fired as of today.

269
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:04,870
What?

270
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:07,873
Why…

271
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,251
You're firing me?

272
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:13,962
Your drama's at a crucial stage, right?

273
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:16,215
You think about it day and night.

274
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:18,217
Well, yeah, it's a crucial time.

275
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,761
But did you really have to fire me?

276
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:22,846
This is making me uncomfortable.

277
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:26,141
I only hired you as my secretary
to fool Choi Do-yoon.

278
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:29,853
You've worked for over two months.
That should be enough.

279
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:33,106
Still, this is all so sudden.

280
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:38,195
The whole point of our arrangement
was so you could write your script.

281
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:39,863
That has to come first.

282
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:46,620
I'll have Mr. Yoon explain things
to the other secretaries.

283
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:49,414
Don't worry. Just focus on your script.

284
00:20:49,998 --> 00:20:51,667
Thanks for being so considerate.

285
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:57,047
Ms. Writer Na Bo-bae.

286
00:20:57,714 --> 00:21:00,300
I'm off to work. See you later.

287
00:21:00,384 --> 00:21:03,220
Take your time and finish this.

288
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:21,989
What was that? Honestly.

289
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,415
Firing her was the right decision.

290
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:34,584
It's too risky to keep Ms. Na around.

291
00:21:35,877 --> 00:21:36,837
What risk?

292
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:39,047
Once the contract ends, you'll part ways.

293
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:44,386
This is a perfectly natural way
to gradually cut ties with her.

294
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:46,930
What are you talking about?
Why would I do that?

295
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:49,558
I'm going to keep seeing her
after our contract ends.

296
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,101
Are you really dating her?

297
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:53,395
Watch the road or we'll crash!

298
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:54,438
Yes, sir.

299
00:22:00,777 --> 00:22:01,695
That's right.

300
00:22:01,778 --> 00:22:04,406
I'm dating Ms. Na Bo-bae.

301
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:11,246
Mr. Yoon, have you lost your mind?

302
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,247
I'm sorry.

303
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:13,999
I thought I saw something ahead.

304
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:16,251
Be careful.

305
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:18,253
My heart can't take it.

306
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:21,340
I'm sorry.

307
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:38,023
Hey!

308
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:44,196
Does that have caffeine in it?

309
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:45,739
It's decaf.

310
00:22:45,822 --> 00:22:48,575
Don't lie to me.
I felt the caffeine on my tongue!

311
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:51,161
Don't you know I have trouble sleeping?

312
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:53,789
Decaf, please!

313
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:55,624
Yes, ma'am. I'm sorry.

314
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:57,125
Unbelievable.

315
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:04,883
Hi, Mom. What's up?

316
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:07,928
A ledger?

317
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:12,766
What? Do…

318
00:23:13,266 --> 00:23:15,227
Doseong Daily?

319
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,814
Do you admit to the charges?

320
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:42,421
Breaking news.
Through Doseong Daily, JBS has obtained

321
00:23:42,504 --> 00:23:46,258
the TS Hotel slush fund ledger mentioned
by Senior Managing Director Baek Ho-rang

322
00:23:46,341 --> 00:23:49,010
at TS Resort's emergency press conference.

323
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:51,263
Assemblyman Choi Tae-sik
was found to have fabricated

324
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:53,765
the allegation
that Mr. Baek mistreated people.

325
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:57,519
Meanwhile, the dispute
over the TS Group succession continues.

326
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:59,396
We'll keep you updated as more…

327
00:23:59,479 --> 00:24:00,355
Baek Ho-rang.

328
00:24:01,356 --> 00:24:04,025
So this was your trump card?

329
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:05,861
Baek Ho-rang!

330
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:09,656
Sir.

331
00:24:09,739 --> 00:24:11,199
Move. You son of a bitch!

332
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:19,249
Mr. Choi.

333
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:22,961
Call security.

334
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:24,504
They're coming.

335
00:24:25,088 --> 00:24:27,841
Why'd you only get my dad arrested?

336
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:29,843
Why leave my mom and me out of it?

337
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:32,804
Are you trying to humiliate me?

338
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:36,641
Let go.

339
00:24:37,559 --> 00:24:38,852
Okay.

340
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:46,359
You can't be that dumb.

341
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:50,822
We have to get through
TS's 30th anniversary party scandal-free.

342
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:52,616
Just hang tight.

343
00:24:52,699 --> 00:24:56,203
I'll take care of the two of you
once it's over.

344
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:57,787
Take care of us?

345
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:08,882
This is

346
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,134
all you can do.

347
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:14,387
Cursing, spitting, making a scene.

348
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:16,181
That's just your level.

349
00:25:17,057 --> 00:25:21,228
Did you really think you and your family
could get your hands on TS?

350
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:22,145
Yeah.

351
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:25,565
At least my family isn't dead.

352
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:30,153
We're alive,
so we can at least put up a fight.

353
00:25:30,654 --> 00:25:31,696
Instead of coming to me,

354
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:34,991
go whine to your family

355
00:25:35,575 --> 00:25:36,826
while they're still alive.

356
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:40,956
And you should take good care
of Na Bo-bae.

357
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:45,043
Everyone you care about ends up dead,
don't they?

358
00:25:45,544 --> 00:25:47,921
Who knows? Na Bo-bae might also--

359
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:56,763
Don't you dare

360
00:25:58,265 --> 00:26:00,308
drag Ms. Na into this.

361
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:02,727
Sir, that's enough.

362
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:09,526
-Clean this mess up.
-Yes, sir.

363
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:15,198
I have to go see my grandmother.

364
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:22,080
How did you like the show I put on?

365
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:24,583
The real embezzler has been exposed,

366
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:26,543
the stock price is recovering,

367
00:26:27,127 --> 00:26:33,008
and thanks to the Ji Eun-ho incident,
public opinion of TS Resort has improved.

368
00:26:33,091 --> 00:26:35,051
Patting yourself on the back, huh?

369
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:37,637
Aren't you happy?

370
00:26:38,346 --> 00:26:40,265
I even took care of Uncle,

371
00:26:40,348 --> 00:26:42,892
who was a thorn in your side.

372
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:50,400
At the upcoming 30th anniversary party,

373
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:57,032
earn everyone's respect with
those abilities you keep bragging about.

374
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:04,706
Very well.

375
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:07,584
See you at the party.

376
00:27:27,687 --> 00:27:28,772
You're here.

377
00:27:30,398 --> 00:27:32,150
I'm home.

378
00:27:32,901 --> 00:27:33,777
Come with me.

379
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:35,445
Huh? What is it?

380
00:27:37,030 --> 00:27:38,073
What is it?

381
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:42,118
"We're at the office. Are you crazy?"

382
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:47,582
-Do I have to?
-Come on. Just do it.

383
00:27:57,258 --> 00:27:58,760
"I don't care

384
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:02,263
if we're at the office or on the street."

385
00:28:03,098 --> 00:28:05,767
"All I see is you, ma'am."

386
00:28:11,314 --> 00:28:12,482
Are you kidding me?

387
00:28:15,610 --> 00:28:16,903
That's not in the script.

388
00:28:16,986 --> 00:28:19,364
No, I'm asking if you're messing with me.

389
00:28:19,989 --> 00:28:21,866
You can't read the lines like that.

390
00:28:21,950 --> 00:28:24,869
You need to put some feeling into it
and make it sound real.

391
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,913
You're not helping at all.

392
00:28:26,996 --> 00:28:28,206
Am I an actor?

393
00:28:28,289 --> 00:28:30,208
I'm just a senior managing director.

394
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:33,878
I just have to read the lines.
Do I have to put emotion into it too?

395
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:37,382
Eun-ho was always great at this.
I wish I could call him.

396
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:38,675
What?

397
00:28:38,758 --> 00:28:40,593
Why'd you have to bring him up?

398
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:42,345
He's an actor, and I'm--

399
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:45,348
Yes, Senior Managing Director
of TS Resort.

400
00:28:45,432 --> 00:28:46,474
Please continue.

401
00:28:50,437 --> 00:28:51,354
I'm not doing it.

402
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,605
Come on. Why?

403
00:28:52,689 --> 00:28:54,399
Don't be like that.

404
00:28:54,482 --> 00:28:57,026
Just read it once. Hurry.

405
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:59,654
The other day at work, you were like,

406
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:02,115
"Will you go out with me?"

407
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:04,284
I told you to forget about that.

408
00:29:06,286 --> 00:29:09,289
I know you can do a good job.
That's why I'm pushing you.

409
00:29:09,372 --> 00:29:10,832
Just try it one more time.

410
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:13,168
"I don't care

411
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:16,296
if we're at the office or on the street."

412
00:29:16,379 --> 00:29:20,175
"All I see is you, ma'am!"

413
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:24,846
Mom.

414
00:29:25,346 --> 00:29:26,806
Mom, it's a misunderstanding.

415
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:30,518
You know he's a man of integrity.

416
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:33,855
He's a four-term assemblyman
and a presidential front-runner.

417
00:29:33,938 --> 00:29:35,064
Do you think…

418
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:39,569
I'll go easy on you
because you're my daughter?

419
00:29:40,737 --> 00:29:43,198
This isn't the time
to be defending your husband.

420
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:48,745
Why can't you go easy on me?

421
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,956
How can you treat me worse than a dog?

422
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,792
You trust your dead son more than me?

423
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:56,544
Do you care more about Lucky Charm,
that damn dog, than me?

424
00:29:57,128 --> 00:29:58,046
Of course.

425
00:30:00,715 --> 00:30:01,549
What did you say?

426
00:30:02,133 --> 00:30:06,012
If Gyeong-seok were still alive,
I would have retired a long time ago.

427
00:30:06,095 --> 00:30:09,474
He was sharp at his job
and had the guts to think big.

428
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:13,311
Obviously, you're no match
for Gyeong-seok.

429
00:30:14,729 --> 00:30:18,024
You know, I expected more from you
because you're my daughter.

430
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:22,153
But Gyeong-seok was the one
who took after me,

431
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:23,488
not you.

432
00:30:25,156 --> 00:30:27,534
Do I care more about my dog than you?

433
00:30:28,409 --> 00:30:32,622
He does exactly what I say.
He even plays dead when I tell him to.

434
00:30:33,456 --> 00:30:35,834
He's cute and does adorable things.

435
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:37,252
But you…

436
00:30:38,962 --> 00:30:42,257
You flounder through life,
consumed by your insecurities.

437
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:43,299
It's pathetic.

438
00:30:44,050 --> 00:30:47,470
You're foolish, can't do anything right,

439
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:50,515
and you married a man just like you.

440
00:30:51,724 --> 00:30:52,684
Do I…

441
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:57,272
Do I have to be good at everything?
Do I have to be perfect?

442
00:30:57,355 --> 00:30:58,523
I'm your daughter!

443
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:02,986
Please, Mom! Please!

444
00:31:03,069 --> 00:31:08,783
Can you stop treating me as a racehorse
and see me as your daughter for once?

445
00:31:10,201 --> 00:31:13,079
Do you even know
why I've been insecure my whole life?

446
00:31:13,162 --> 00:31:16,499
It's all because of you!
This is how I was raised!

447
00:31:17,709 --> 00:31:19,085
Gyeong-jin.

448
00:31:20,628 --> 00:31:23,756
You resent me, don't you?
Maybe even hate me.

449
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:29,262
You must wonder how it's possible
for a mother to be like this.

450
00:31:31,264 --> 00:31:32,473
But…

451
00:31:36,019 --> 00:31:36,936
I feel the same way.

452
00:31:39,397 --> 00:31:41,566
I resent you too.

453
00:31:41,649 --> 00:31:43,318
I hate the sight of you.

454
00:31:45,111 --> 00:31:48,489
Why is the only child I have left
so disappointing?

455
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:51,451
I miss Gyeong-seok so much it hurts.

456
00:31:56,706 --> 00:31:57,999
You're unbelievable.

457
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:06,049
What was I expecting?

458
00:32:08,426 --> 00:32:09,844
From Chairwoman Gong Man-seol.

459
00:32:11,179 --> 00:32:14,265
You, Choi Tae-sik, and Do-yoon…

460
00:32:14,807 --> 00:32:17,310
Get ready to return
everything you've received.

461
00:32:48,216 --> 00:32:49,467
Mr. Baek Ho-rang!

462
00:32:50,176 --> 00:32:51,427
Yes? What is it?

463
00:32:51,511 --> 00:32:52,929
-Look at this.
-Huh?

464
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:54,222
CHOI TAE-SIK ARRESTED

465
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:57,225
-Your name is cleared, right?
-It was all over the news yesterday.

466
00:32:57,308 --> 00:33:00,478
-You didn't know?
-I was busy writing my script.

467
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:02,897
Why didn't you tell me?
This is great news!

468
00:33:02,981 --> 00:33:04,357
You knew this would happen.

469
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:05,566
Yeah, but still…

470
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:08,861
Sit down. Charge me.

471
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:15,493
Huh?

472
00:33:15,576 --> 00:33:16,828
You're fully charged.

473
00:33:18,579 --> 00:33:23,292
We still have to do the morning charge.
It's in the contract.

474
00:33:23,376 --> 00:33:25,962
What? There's no such thing.

475
00:33:26,963 --> 00:33:28,464
You don't want to hold hands?

476
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:31,092
No, it's not that I don't want to.

477
00:33:31,718 --> 00:33:35,888
You could just ask me to hold your hand
instead of using charging as an excuse.

478
00:33:40,852 --> 00:33:41,686
Then…

479
00:33:44,063 --> 00:33:45,314
let's keep holding hands.

480
00:33:49,986 --> 00:33:51,112
Okay.

481
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:55,885
-What?
-Nothing.

482
00:35:01,432 --> 00:35:03,434
Why are you trying to pull your hand away?

483
00:35:03,935 --> 00:35:05,061
Someone's walking by.

484
00:35:05,144 --> 00:35:08,689
Wow, it's obvious
you've never been in a relationship.

485
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:12,193
Is holding hands really that embarrassing?

486
00:35:12,276 --> 00:35:15,154
Not really, but it's kind of… you know.

487
00:35:15,738 --> 00:35:18,574
So what, you've been
in lots of relationships?

488
00:35:18,658 --> 00:35:21,369
A few girls flirted with you.
That's about it.

489
00:35:21,869 --> 00:35:24,831
It's not like you have
a lot of dating experience either.

490
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:27,083
Maybe not, but definitely more than you.

491
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:34,090
Oh, how many?

492
00:35:34,173 --> 00:35:35,424
What?

493
00:35:36,926 --> 00:35:37,969
Oh.

494
00:35:39,428 --> 00:35:40,346
Not that many.

495
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:42,306
Not many at all.

496
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:44,767
You're my first, Ms. Na Bo-bae.

497
00:35:45,351 --> 00:35:46,435
Watch what you say.

498
00:35:47,311 --> 00:35:48,146
I will.

499
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:00,783
I've never done this with anyone before.

500
00:36:00,867 --> 00:36:02,243
Kissing on the street.

501
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:07,165
And

502
00:36:07,665 --> 00:36:08,749
this too.

503
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:11,127
-Huh? What are you doing?
-It's a first for me.

504
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:13,087
Put me down!

505
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:16,507
You know I have a weak heart,
so stay still.

506
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:38,112
Should we

507
00:36:39,071 --> 00:36:40,156
hurry home?

508
00:36:41,574 --> 00:36:42,700
Yes.

509
00:36:50,666 --> 00:36:53,753
Hi, Seol-hee. What's up?
You came all the way to see me?

510
00:36:53,836 --> 00:36:55,421
I'll have what he's having.

511
00:36:58,549 --> 00:37:01,135
I've got a reason to drink,

512
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:03,804
but why is my dear Seol-hee
in such a bad mood?

513
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:05,514
Oh.

514
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:08,643
Your cousin and grandma

515
00:37:09,185 --> 00:37:10,728
ruined my mood.

516
00:37:12,855 --> 00:37:13,856
What?

517
00:37:14,982 --> 00:37:18,236
I said it'd be best if you gave up now.

518
00:37:19,195 --> 00:37:20,112
But ma'am…

519
00:37:20,196 --> 00:37:22,782
I was quite fond of you.

520
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:27,328
I thought it was cute
that you pretended to be gentle and kind.

521
00:37:27,411 --> 00:37:31,374
I thought you'd make
a good daughter-in-law for the TS family.

522
00:37:32,959 --> 00:37:35,211
And seeing how you grew your company,

523
00:37:35,294 --> 00:37:37,505
I thought you could help Ho-rang.

524
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:41,717
Don't look so upset. It's a compliment.

525
00:37:42,718 --> 00:37:45,680
All your compliments
are in the past tense.

526
00:37:45,763 --> 00:37:47,890
Even if it's all in the past,

527
00:37:47,974 --> 00:37:51,435
it's still a huge compliment
that I trusted you, isn't it?

528
00:37:53,980 --> 00:37:55,106
But

529
00:37:56,107 --> 00:38:00,236
Ho-rang proved his worth
without your help.

530
00:38:04,073 --> 00:38:05,157
Drink up.

531
00:38:08,577 --> 00:38:12,290
So does that mean
you don't need me anymore?

532
00:38:12,373 --> 00:38:15,251
I have no reason to pressure him
into marriage anymore, so--

533
00:38:15,334 --> 00:38:16,460
If you give me another--

534
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:19,672
You know it's not up to me
to give you another chance, right?

535
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:25,177
The tea tastes bitter today.

536
00:38:25,261 --> 00:38:27,388
I don't think you should drink it.

537
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:35,813
Relying on an old hag
could only get me so far.

538
00:38:39,775 --> 00:38:42,903
Do-yoon, you have
someone tailing Baek Ho-rang, right?

539
00:38:42,987 --> 00:38:44,030
Huh?

540
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:45,823
Yeah.

541
00:38:45,906 --> 00:38:49,744
I've always had someone tailing him.

542
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:52,538
Then

543
00:38:53,039 --> 00:38:55,750
you must know a thing or two
about Na Bo-bae.

544
00:38:57,918 --> 00:39:02,798
Interesting to hear you
bring up Na Bo-bae.

545
00:39:13,559 --> 00:39:15,519
I was taught

546
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:19,273
to do my best to protect myself.

547
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:26,322
Why don't we come up with a Plan B?

548
00:39:29,283 --> 00:39:31,994
CARDIOTHORACIC SURGERY
JANG KI-WOOK

549
00:40:01,357 --> 00:40:03,109
MEDICAL RECORD
BAEK HO-RANG

550
00:40:05,069 --> 00:40:07,196
So he had surgery,

551
00:40:07,696 --> 00:40:09,532
but the cardiac device failed

552
00:40:09,615 --> 00:40:12,034
because of a power outage?

553
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:19,750
INPATIENT RECORD
NA BO-BAE

554
00:40:19,834 --> 00:40:21,001
What's this?

555
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:24,547
"Cardiac arrest due to lightning strike"?

556
00:40:24,630 --> 00:40:27,341
Look at you giving your name
without a shred of shame.

557
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:35,433
Wait a minute.

558
00:40:38,185 --> 00:40:39,979
L

559
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,442
Hey, it's me.

560
00:40:44,942 --> 00:40:48,112
Have you ever seen
Na Bo-bae and Baek Ho-rang holding hands

561
00:40:48,195 --> 00:40:49,738
or touching each other at all?

562
00:40:50,656 --> 00:40:52,908
Damn. You're useless.

563
00:40:54,326 --> 00:40:56,370
I'll see for myself.

564
00:40:57,830 --> 00:41:00,833
Wow, look. It must be on sale.

565
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:02,042
-Yeah?
-Looks good, huh?

566
00:41:02,126 --> 00:41:03,169
Looks pretty unhealthy.

567
00:41:03,252 --> 00:41:06,755
Come on. We don't have any snacks at home.

568
00:41:06,839 --> 00:41:08,632
Looks like buy one, get one free.

569
00:41:08,716 --> 00:41:10,676
-I don't think so.
-Let's get this.

570
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:15,306
Wait.

571
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:19,310
Yes, Director.

572
00:41:19,393 --> 00:41:22,396
Ms. Na, I read the revised script.

573
00:41:23,189 --> 00:41:24,315
It's good.

574
00:41:24,398 --> 00:41:25,774
-Really?
-Yeah.

575
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:27,776
Wanna hear some more good news?

576
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:30,196
We have a meeting with the female lead.

577
00:41:30,988 --> 00:41:32,406
The actress playing Hye-ju?

578
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:35,993
Yeah, Yoo Min-hee accepted the part.

579
00:41:36,785 --> 00:41:39,747
Yoo Min-hee? Isn't she a huge star?

580
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:42,041
Of course she is. She's a superstar.

581
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:43,751
She loves the script.

582
00:41:43,834 --> 00:41:45,836
-She wants to meet next week.
-Really?

583
00:41:46,754 --> 00:41:48,631
Yes. Got it!

584
00:41:48,714 --> 00:41:49,548
Okay.

585
00:41:50,090 --> 00:41:51,258
No way!

586
00:41:51,342 --> 00:41:53,052
-This is insane!
-What is it?

587
00:41:53,636 --> 00:41:55,262
We've got our female lead.

588
00:41:55,888 --> 00:41:56,931
Yoo Min-hee.

589
00:41:59,975 --> 00:42:02,686
-Who is Yoo Min-hee?
-You don't know who she is?

590
00:42:03,646 --> 00:42:06,190
Don't you watch TV?

591
00:42:06,732 --> 00:42:08,359
-TV?
-Yeah.

592
00:42:08,442 --> 00:42:12,696
-Come on. How do you not know?
-So nothing happens when he touches her.

593
00:42:14,490 --> 00:42:16,742
That patient, Na Bo-bae,
was a little strange.

594
00:42:16,825 --> 00:42:18,619
Lots of static electricity.

595
00:42:19,286 --> 00:42:21,539
Mr. Baek's heart had run out of battery,

596
00:42:22,122 --> 00:42:24,291
but it recharged when he was near Ms. Na.

597
00:42:25,376 --> 00:42:28,003
So she really is a human charger.

598
00:42:36,887 --> 00:42:38,514
Someone's over the moon, huh?

599
00:42:39,014 --> 00:42:41,517
Yoo Min-hee's going to star in my show.

600
00:42:42,017 --> 00:42:43,018
Am I dreaming?

601
00:42:43,519 --> 00:42:45,062
Can I pinch your cheek?

602
00:42:45,145 --> 00:42:48,190
Why would you pinch me?
Shouldn't it be the other way round?

603
00:42:48,274 --> 00:42:49,650
I guess it's not a dream.

604
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:53,737
I knew you wouldn't agree to be pinched.
You're too protective of yourself.

605
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:55,531
What did you say?

606
00:42:56,115 --> 00:43:00,035
Now we just need the male lead.
I hope they cast a really handsome actor.

607
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:04,623
Why do you care if the actor's handsome?

608
00:43:04,707 --> 00:43:07,167
People watch romance dramas
for the handsome male leads.

609
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:09,044
That's the bare minimum.

610
00:43:11,380 --> 00:43:14,049
You're not casting Mr. Ji Eun-ho
as the male lead, are you?

611
00:43:14,133 --> 00:43:17,011
Eun-ho? Isn't that kind of a long shot?

612
00:43:18,012 --> 00:43:20,723
I mean, the rumors have been cleared up,

613
00:43:20,806 --> 00:43:22,850
but our names were linked and all.

614
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:26,353
I don't want him
to get caught up in all that again.

615
00:43:29,023 --> 00:43:30,107
Whatever.

616
00:43:41,744 --> 00:43:44,747
You're the only one I'm interested in,
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

617
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:47,958
So stop being jealous over nothing.

618
00:43:58,135 --> 00:43:59,970
She drives me crazy.

619
00:44:01,597 --> 00:44:02,973
Clear your mind

620
00:44:03,682 --> 00:44:05,309
of distracting thoughts

621
00:44:06,477 --> 00:44:07,645
and worries.

622
00:44:41,595 --> 00:44:42,805
Hey, Ji-hye.

623
00:44:46,308 --> 00:44:47,393
What did you say?

624
00:44:58,237 --> 00:45:00,364
Yong-gi! Ji-hye.

625
00:45:00,447 --> 00:45:01,407
Hey.

626
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:05,160
What happened? Was it a hit-and-run?

627
00:45:05,244 --> 00:45:07,287
A car hit him in an alley and drove off.

628
00:45:07,371 --> 00:45:08,747
How badly are you hurt?

629
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:10,999
Just a broken arm. That's all.

630
00:45:11,083 --> 00:45:13,711
I don't even need surgery.
I'll be out in two days.

631
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:17,005
But how are you going to train
with a broken arm?

632
00:45:17,089 --> 00:45:18,257
What about your dojo?

633
00:45:19,466 --> 00:45:21,969
I already closed it down.

634
00:45:22,511 --> 00:45:24,138
You did? When?

635
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:28,100
He closed it down a while ago.

636
00:45:28,183 --> 00:45:31,562
He stuck around
because he didn't want you to be alone

637
00:45:31,645 --> 00:45:34,064
if you gave up writing
and moved back to Daejeon.

638
00:45:34,148 --> 00:45:36,483
Bo-bae, you're turning 30 soon.

639
00:45:36,567 --> 00:45:40,112
I'm so happy you renewed your contract
and have your own studio now.

640
00:45:40,195 --> 00:45:42,948
I'm glad I can move back to Daejeon
on my own now.

641
00:45:44,366 --> 00:45:45,951
Good for you.

642
00:45:46,452 --> 00:45:49,538
Eat the bone broth I made
and get well soon.

643
00:45:49,621 --> 00:45:51,498
Don't make Mom and Dad look after you.

644
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:53,208
If you're gonna nag, go home.

645
00:45:55,002 --> 00:45:55,836
Sit down.

646
00:45:55,919 --> 00:45:57,129
Okay.

647
00:45:57,629 --> 00:45:58,589
Have you eaten?

648
00:45:58,672 --> 00:46:00,007
I'm good.

649
00:46:00,090 --> 00:46:02,551
-Want something to drink?
-No, I'm good.

650
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:10,100
Bo-bae, you're turning 30 soon.

651
00:46:10,184 --> 00:46:13,437
I'm so happy you renewed your contract
and have your own studio now.

652
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:16,190
I'm glad I can move back to Daejeon
on my own now.

653
00:46:16,690 --> 00:46:20,694
The show's been scheduled,
and the female lead's been cast.

654
00:46:21,487 --> 00:46:23,238
I'm not lying.

655
00:46:26,158 --> 00:46:27,242
You're here…

656
00:47:02,444 --> 00:47:04,363
Where did Na Yong-gi go?

657
00:47:04,446 --> 00:47:06,031
-Are you his guardian?
-Yes.

658
00:47:06,114 --> 00:47:07,574
Mr. Na Yong-gi…

659
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:09,993
He was moved to a VIP room two hours ago.

660
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:12,579
A VIP room?

661
00:47:14,289 --> 00:47:16,583
Come on. Just a little longer!

662
00:47:16,667 --> 00:47:18,544
Is this even hard?

663
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:21,839
You need to have a strong core, you know?

664
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:22,798
It's been a minute!

665
00:47:22,881 --> 00:47:24,591
-Yeah, squeeze your glutes.
-Squeeze!

666
00:47:24,675 --> 00:47:26,552
What are you guys doing?

667
00:47:26,635 --> 00:47:28,011
-Bo-bae.
-Hey, Bo-bae.

668
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:29,263
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

669
00:47:31,890 --> 00:47:34,601
-Seriously?
-We haven't done much, Bo-bae.

670
00:47:34,685 --> 00:47:37,563
-Just small talk.
-Yeah! What's the big deal?

671
00:47:38,188 --> 00:47:39,439
We were just talking.

672
00:47:42,526 --> 00:47:44,653
We didn't really talk.

673
00:47:48,198 --> 00:47:49,908
You're impossible.

674
00:47:49,992 --> 00:47:51,076
Huh?

675
00:47:52,369 --> 00:47:55,372
-You were at the café.
-Hello, I'm Baek Ho-rang.

676
00:47:55,455 --> 00:47:56,290
I see.

677
00:47:58,333 --> 00:48:00,335
I heard you upgraded my room.

678
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:02,129
Who exactly are you?

679
00:48:02,212 --> 00:48:04,548
Well, Ms. Na Bo-bae and I are--

680
00:48:04,631 --> 00:48:06,508
Silence! I do not wish to hear it.

681
00:48:06,592 --> 00:48:08,176
Why are you talking like that?

682
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:15,559
You're so handsome.

683
00:48:16,059 --> 00:48:17,144
Handsome, my ass.

684
00:48:18,186 --> 00:48:22,232
Didn't you say
you met Bo-bae at the hospital?

685
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:24,818
Is everything okay with you?

686
00:48:25,402 --> 00:48:27,779
Oh, back then…

687
00:48:28,822 --> 00:48:31,825
Well, I was there for a checkup.

688
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:33,493
How much do you make?

689
00:48:33,577 --> 00:48:34,995
Hey!

690
00:48:35,078 --> 00:48:37,456
Why are you asking him that?

691
00:48:37,539 --> 00:48:38,916
What's your net worth?

692
00:48:39,583 --> 00:48:41,710
Do you work out?

693
00:48:41,793 --> 00:48:44,129
Yes, I do yoga.

694
00:48:46,006 --> 00:48:47,257
Yoga?

695
00:48:48,342 --> 00:48:51,595
I heard yoga is good
for cardiovascular health.

696
00:48:57,517 --> 00:48:58,518
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

697
00:49:07,986 --> 00:49:10,364
Why would you put up with all that?

698
00:49:10,447 --> 00:49:13,283
You're usually good at saying no,
like a real douchebag.

699
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:14,701
When was I ever a…

700
00:49:17,955 --> 00:49:19,915
When was I ever a douchebag?

701
00:49:19,998 --> 00:49:21,416
And you guys.

702
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:25,003
Why would you make someone
with heart issues do planks?

703
00:49:25,087 --> 00:49:26,713
-Heart?
-He has heart issues?

704
00:49:31,343 --> 00:49:32,177
I mean,

705
00:49:32,761 --> 00:49:34,346
his heart…

706
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:37,641
You know, his heart. His feelings.

707
00:49:37,724 --> 00:49:39,810
His heart is under stress.

708
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:41,478
He's been busy with work.

709
00:49:42,062 --> 00:49:44,356
-He's under a lot of stress.
-I'm so stressed.

710
00:49:44,439 --> 00:49:45,816
His heart's under stress.

711
00:49:46,400 --> 00:49:49,236
Exactly. You can relieve stress
by working out.

712
00:49:49,319 --> 00:49:53,281
But why would you two help him
relieve his stress?

713
00:49:55,283 --> 00:49:56,535
Let me see.

714
00:49:56,618 --> 00:49:57,744
-Bo-bae!
-No!

715
00:50:04,835 --> 00:50:07,587
My electricity doesn't affect him.

716
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:08,672
What?

717
00:50:09,798 --> 00:50:11,508
What? It doesn't affect him?

718
00:50:13,010 --> 00:50:14,845
This punk knows about your powers?

719
00:50:15,637 --> 00:50:17,264
Yeah, he knows.

720
00:50:17,931 --> 00:50:20,767
I can touch his bare skin like this,
and nothing happens.

721
00:50:21,977 --> 00:50:23,061
-Yes.
-Yeah.

722
00:50:24,396 --> 00:50:26,106
-But…
-I'm fine.

723
00:50:26,189 --> 00:50:27,399
-But how…
-That's…

724
00:50:27,482 --> 00:50:29,359
Come on. Let me see.

725
00:50:29,443 --> 00:50:31,194
Did you overdo it? Are you okay?

726
00:50:32,529 --> 00:50:33,363
I'm fine.

727
00:50:33,447 --> 00:50:36,908
Yoga's actually harder than planks.

728
00:50:37,409 --> 00:50:38,577
What's going on?

729
00:50:38,660 --> 00:50:40,245
-The electricity…
-I'm fine.

730
00:50:40,328 --> 00:50:41,705
Why are you fine?

731
00:50:48,128 --> 00:50:51,048
How did you know
my brother was in the hospital?

732
00:50:53,425 --> 00:50:56,386
Why didn't you tell me?

733
00:50:57,888 --> 00:50:58,805
I just…

734
00:50:59,431 --> 00:51:01,099
It's a family matter.

735
00:51:01,600 --> 00:51:05,771
You were already busy,
so I didn't want to bother you.

736
00:51:08,398 --> 00:51:10,859
Wow, I'm so hurt.

737
00:51:10,942 --> 00:51:12,027
What?

738
00:51:12,110 --> 00:51:13,612
It really hurts…

739
00:51:16,156 --> 00:51:18,325
that my heart's aching.

740
00:51:18,408 --> 00:51:20,744
I mean, it's not really that…

741
00:51:22,079 --> 00:51:23,205
Is it because of the planks?

742
00:51:25,123 --> 00:51:29,586
My heart starts to ache
when I'm worried or anxious.

743
00:51:30,295 --> 00:51:34,007
I start imagining all kinds of things
that could go wrong.

744
00:51:34,758 --> 00:51:35,801
Right now,

745
00:51:36,384 --> 00:51:40,889
it hurts so much
that you didn't rely on me.

746
00:51:42,849 --> 00:51:45,227
It makes me wonder if you don't trust me.

747
00:51:45,811 --> 00:51:48,396
It's not that I don't trust you.

748
00:51:49,481 --> 00:51:50,315
I just…

749
00:51:51,441 --> 00:51:53,527
It's because I like you so much.

750
00:51:54,611 --> 00:51:58,657
I didn't want to make you worry
or burden you with my problems.

751
00:51:59,574 --> 00:52:02,661
You already have enough to worry about.

752
00:52:09,167 --> 00:52:11,211
What are you doing all of a sudden?

753
00:52:14,965 --> 00:52:15,799
Are you crazy?

754
00:52:15,882 --> 00:52:19,052
I think I finally understand
why you called me cute.

755
00:52:19,886 --> 00:52:21,930
You're really cute.

756
00:52:22,013 --> 00:52:23,598
Seriously…

757
00:52:28,436 --> 00:52:31,815
So you didn't want me to worry
because you like me?

758
00:52:32,357 --> 00:52:35,318
You said you felt hurt
because I didn't rely on you.

759
00:52:35,402 --> 00:52:36,987
I think that's adorable too.

760
00:52:41,491 --> 00:52:45,871
Let me be a part of your life from now on.

761
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:50,917
When someone in your family is sick,
let me know.

762
00:52:51,001 --> 00:52:54,588
And if something goes wrong,
we'll get through it together.

763
00:52:58,675 --> 00:53:00,468
Let's do it together. You and me.

764
00:53:01,344 --> 00:53:02,929
Together?

765
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:05,432
Yeah. Together.

766
00:53:18,153 --> 00:53:19,154
Well…

767
00:53:20,280 --> 00:53:21,740
Anyway,

768
00:53:22,407 --> 00:53:25,202
TS's 30th anniversary party

769
00:53:25,827 --> 00:53:27,370
is coming up.

770
00:53:28,163 --> 00:53:29,122
Would you…

771
00:53:32,500 --> 00:53:35,378
like to go with me?

772
00:53:39,049 --> 00:53:41,134
Is this what you were building up to?

773
00:53:42,385 --> 00:53:44,262
Sure. I'll go with you.

774
00:53:45,096 --> 00:53:46,056
We'll go together.

775
00:53:48,183 --> 00:53:49,226
Together?

776
00:53:50,518 --> 00:53:51,686
Together.

777
00:54:11,915 --> 00:54:13,291
-Welcome.
-Welcome.

778
00:54:13,375 --> 00:54:15,043
This way, please.

779
00:54:32,269 --> 00:54:35,605
Sorry, I don't really like
people touching my bare skin.

780
00:54:36,940 --> 00:54:39,567
We can't do your makeup without--

781
00:54:39,651 --> 00:54:41,027
-Ma'am.
-Yes?

782
00:54:43,238 --> 00:54:45,365
-Please take good care of her.
-Of course.

783
00:54:49,411 --> 00:54:50,412
Thank you.

784
00:55:35,248 --> 00:55:36,291
Let's go.

785
00:55:38,585 --> 00:55:40,253
You don't seem impressed.

786
00:55:40,337 --> 00:55:41,171
It's Mr. Baek

787
00:55:42,005 --> 00:55:43,340
you want to impress.

788
00:55:45,342 --> 00:55:47,635
Why isn't Mr. Baek coming with us?

789
00:55:47,719 --> 00:55:50,472
He's already there, waiting for you.

790
00:55:52,849 --> 00:55:53,892
Thank you.

791
00:55:54,809 --> 00:55:55,769
Let's go.

792
00:56:13,536 --> 00:56:16,706
It seems like it's just about confirmed.

793
00:56:17,207 --> 00:56:19,292
With Assemblyman Choi Tae-sik arrested…

794
00:56:19,376 --> 00:56:20,668
That's right.

795
00:56:20,752 --> 00:56:23,588
Maybe that's why
you're positively glowing today, Mr. Baek.

796
00:56:23,671 --> 00:56:26,383
You should be the face of the brand
instead of Ji Eun-ho.

797
00:56:26,466 --> 00:56:29,469
-Well, aren't you a smooth talker?
-That's right.

798
00:56:40,814 --> 00:56:41,731
Thank you.

799
00:56:43,775 --> 00:56:45,443
Is everything all right?

800
00:56:45,527 --> 00:56:46,403
Yes.

801
00:56:46,486 --> 00:56:47,320
Oh.

802
00:56:49,030 --> 00:56:50,573
Can I drink this water?

803
00:56:50,657 --> 00:56:53,201
Yes. We'll be on our way now.

804
00:56:53,284 --> 00:56:54,119
Okay.

805
00:57:16,266 --> 00:57:18,935
PORTABLE CHARGER

806
00:57:29,154 --> 00:57:31,406
MR. YOON

807
00:57:44,919 --> 00:57:46,337
What are you doing here?

808
00:57:48,506 --> 00:57:49,340
Oh, hello.

809
00:57:49,424 --> 00:57:52,302
You said you had a date.
Why are you here alone?

810
00:57:52,927 --> 00:57:54,429
She's on her way.

811
00:57:54,929 --> 00:57:57,390
Then let's chat until she gets here.

812
00:57:59,017 --> 00:58:00,560
The marriage isn't happening,

813
00:58:00,643 --> 00:58:03,688
but we still need to show everyone
TS and Hanlim are on good terms.

814
00:58:05,106 --> 00:58:07,358
The event will begin shortly.

815
00:58:07,442 --> 00:58:09,777
Please take your seats.

816
01:00:09,522 --> 01:00:11,733
Call an ambulance.

817
01:00:12,692 --> 01:00:15,445
No photos. No photos, please!

